1
00:00:22,037 --> 00:00:24,709
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:24,741 --> 00:00:28,477
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:31,061 --> 00:00:40,526
Sharhabil Bin Hasana رضي الله عنه, one of the companions, who led armies against Al-Murtaddeen(ألمرتدين)

4
00:00:43,466 --> 00:00:48,860
came to the Khalifah(خليفه), Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and he said:

5
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:58,106
O Khalifah of Rasool Ullah! Are you thinking about conquering a Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)?

6
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:01,812
Are you thinking about fighting the Romans?

7
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:08,308
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: Yes! I am.

8
00:01:09,856 --> 00:01:14,126
But I've never told anyone about my intentions.

9
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:16,102
So how did you know about it?

10
00:01:17,859 --> 00:01:23,844
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was already thinking about attacking Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

11
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:26,598
He was considering it.

12
00:01:27,955 --> 00:01:37,730
See Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) has been in the Muslim mind since the day Rasool Allah ﷺ made the journey of Al-Isra(ألإسراء).

13
00:01:39,695 --> 00:01:45,266
When Rasool Allah ﷺ went to Jerusalem and he led the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) in a Salah(صلاة).

14
00:01:47,181 --> 00:01:51,572
It was symbolic of Rasool Allah ﷺ receiving the keys to the Holy Land.

15
00:01:51,619 --> 00:01:55,617
Now, you are the inheritor of this blessed land.

16
00:01:55,692 --> 00:01:57,912
الأَرض الَّتِي بَارَكْنَا فِيهَا

17
00:01:57,936 --> 00:02:02,158
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says that, that is the blessed land, mentioned in Qur'an.

18
00:02:04,069 --> 00:02:13,249
So, when Rasool Allah ﷺ goes there and leads the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) whom many of lived in the Holy Land.

19
00:02:14,265 --> 00:02:16,516
 The fact that Rasool Allah ﷺ is leading them

20
00:02:17,266 --> 00:02:24,163
is an indication that Muhammadﷺ now is a new leader, he's the inheritor of the Haqq(حق)

21
00:02:24,659 --> 00:02:26,452
and he is the carrier of the torch.

22
00:02:28,839 --> 00:02:34,582
So even though the Muslims were not incharge of the holy land.

23
00:02:35,884 --> 00:02:41,829
Very early on, they set their sights on Al-Ardh Al-Mubarikah(ألأرض الْمُباركة).

24
00:02:43,309 --> 00:02:50,956
So Rasool Allah ﷺ before he even finishes off the effort of opening Arabia

25
00:02:51,469 --> 00:02:56,524
he's sending an army to Mu'ta(مؤته), deep in the land of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام),

26
00:02:57,084 --> 00:02:58,506
led by Zaid Ibn Harissa(زيد إبن حارثه).

27
00:02:59,162 --> 00:03:04,078
And before that, he has sent a letter to the king of Ghassan(غسَّان),

28
00:03:04,844 --> 00:03:09,172
who when he saw that Muhammadﷺ, this man from Madina is inviting him to Islam,

29
00:03:09,415 --> 00:03:10,464
أسلِم تَسْلَمْ

30
00:03:10,969 --> 00:03:15,846
He became very angry and arrogant, so he wanted to attack Madina.

31
00:03:16,632 --> 00:03:19,001
But the Roman Emperor told him not to do so.

32
00:03:19,398 --> 00:03:25,166
He's the one, who calmed him because the king of Ghassan(غسَّان) his loyalty was to the Roman emperor.

33
00:03:26,627 --> 00:03:33,367
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ in the ninth year, he goes out himself to the Battle of Tabook(تبوك),

34
00:03:33,392 --> 00:03:38,646
which is the borderline between Hijaz(حجاز) and the Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

35
00:03:39,903 --> 00:03:44,886
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ, the following year, gives the banner to Osama Bin Zaid(أسامة بن زيد)

36
00:03:44,910 --> 00:03:48,456
and he dies before Osama(أسامة) goes out, but Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) send him out.

37
00:03:50,921 --> 00:03:55,630
So, the Muslims were thinking about Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) a lot, this is the land of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء),

38
00:03:56,397 --> 00:03:58,456
the Muslims should inherit it.

39
00:04:00,477 --> 00:04:02,337
So, Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة) comes to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

40
00:04:02,361 --> 00:04:03,939
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was thinking about this.

41
00:04:04,572 --> 00:04:06,865
See there was already some things going on.

42
00:04:07,349 --> 00:04:12,592
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) has already sent in Khalid bin Saeed Bin Al-Aas(خالد بن سعيد بن ألعاص) to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

43
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:17,185
But these were small incursions, it wasn't a major campaign.

44
00:04:18,042 --> 00:04:22,104
But now Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) is thinking about an all out assault

45
00:04:22,534 --> 00:04:27,122
on the Roman Empire in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) to take over the land.

46
00:04:27,739 --> 00:04:31,149
It's not just merely sending in, an Army in and out.

47
00:04:31,692 --> 00:04:35,236
So Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة) comes to the Khalifah(خليفه) and says;

48
00:04:36,231 --> 00:04:39,069
Are you thinking about fighting Ar-Rome(ألروم)?

49
00:04:39,815 --> 00:04:41,472
 Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Yes! How did you know?

50
00:04:41,843 --> 00:04:44,145
You only asked me this question because there's a reason.

51
00:04:45,647 --> 00:04:47,995
Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة) said: I saw a dream.

52
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,537
What was a dream?

53
00:04:51,084 --> 00:04:57,260
Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة) said: I saw you walking among the people

54
00:04:59,565 --> 00:05:02,557
and then you climbed over a very rough terrain

55
00:05:05,025 --> 00:05:08,754
and you made your way up to a very high peak.

56
00:05:09,705 --> 00:05:18,478
And then you and your companions took a look from that vantage point to the people under you.

57
00:05:19,994 --> 00:05:27,338
 And then you descended from that peak, into a very fertile plain.

58
00:05:28,863 --> 00:05:35,217
A plain that is lush with vegetation, and it's full of towns and fortresses.

59
00:05:37,573 --> 00:05:42,956
And then you told your companions, to wage war against the enemies of Allah

60
00:05:42,981 --> 00:05:49,734
and I guarantee you victory and booty and you gave me a banner.

61
00:05:50,592 --> 00:05:56,109
And I went ahead with it and I came to a town and the people offered me peace,

62
00:05:56,134 --> 00:06:00,254
so I opened it peacefully and then I came back to you.

63
00:06:01,521 --> 00:06:06,431
And I found you in a very great fortress sitting on a throne

64
00:06:07,032 --> 00:06:12,223
and then a voice came to you and said rejoice with victory

65
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:17,820
so thank Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and then this voice recited to you, Surah An-Nasr(سورةألنصر).

66
00:06:18,543 --> 00:06:20,389
إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ وَالْفَتْحُ ۝

67
00:06:20,762 --> 00:06:23,698
وَرَأَيْتَ النَّاسَ يَدْخُلُونَ فِي دِينِ اللَّهِ أَفْوَاجًا ۝

68
00:06:23,944 --> 00:06:27,865
فَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَاسْتَغْفِرْهُ إِنَّهُ كَانَ تَوَّابًا۝

69
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:36,357
And then I woke up, so that was the end of the dream.

70
00:06:38,274 --> 00:06:41,827
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) with tears swirling in his eyes.

71
00:06:42,702 --> 00:06:52,373
He said: You have given me the glad tidings of opening and also my obituary.

72
00:06:55,237 --> 00:06:58,179
Now Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه used to interpret dreams,

73
00:06:58,511 --> 00:07:00,548
even in the presence of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

74
00:07:02,374 --> 00:07:05,577
Once the dream was presented to Rasool Ullah, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said;

75
00:07:05,602 --> 00:07:07,882
Let me interpret it, O messenger of Allah.

76
00:07:09,461 --> 00:07:11,871
He said: The interpretation of the dream is as follows.

77
00:07:13,219 --> 00:07:16,063
When you saw me climbing a very rough terrain.

78
00:07:17,469 --> 00:07:29,697
This means that me and my soldiers and our enemy are going to have a very rough time in this conflict.

79
00:07:30,215 --> 00:07:32,478
 It's going to be difficult, it's gonna be hard.

80
00:07:34,247 --> 00:07:38,220
Because first you saw him among the people, all people Muslim and non Muslim.

81
00:07:38,865 --> 00:07:42,023
And then Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is now climbing this rough terrain.

82
00:07:44,183 --> 00:07:46,790
So that means it's a very rough conflict.

83
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:52,877
And when you saw me at the top of the mountain,

84
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:59,585
that means in the end, we will prevail, victory will be on our side.

85
00:08:00,170 --> 00:08:03,942
Because now Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is on top, along with his companions, the Muslims

86
00:08:04,606 --> 00:08:10,384
 and the other people are still in the foothills.

87
00:08:11,034 --> 00:08:12,912
And then what was the next part of the dream?

88
00:08:13,475 --> 00:08:16,525
 We came down to a very fertile valley and plain,

89
00:08:17,361 --> 00:08:21,796
lush with vegetation, full of fruits, many towns and fortresses.

90
00:08:22,275 --> 00:08:31,759
He said and that means that after that, we will have a very comfortable living and a luxurious lifestyle.

91
00:08:33,060 --> 00:08:37,037
So after this rough time, of Ghazoo(غزؤ), conquering,

92
00:08:37,532 --> 00:08:41,315
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will make our life very easy, and luxurious.

93
00:08:41,884 --> 00:08:47,955
Many towns, fortresses, vegetation is all under the control of Muslims,

94
00:08:48,083 --> 00:08:50,398
so the Muslim lifestyle will change.

95
00:08:52,088 --> 00:08:55,894
And when you saw me sitting on a throne,

96
00:08:56,654 --> 00:09:03,211
this means that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will make me rise and make the enemies of Allah, Low.

97
00:09:04,693 --> 00:09:09,176
It means that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will make me prevail over the enemies of Allah.

98
00:09:09,768 --> 00:09:11,728
وَرَفَعَ أَبَوَيْهِ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ

99
00:09:12,853 --> 00:09:15,356
It's an indication that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will elevate me.

100
00:09:17,143 --> 00:09:21,622
And then when you heard a voice telling me that you will be victorious,

101
00:09:22,213 --> 00:09:25,226
so thank Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and seek His forgiveness.

102
00:09:26,806 --> 00:09:31,419
This means that my death is approaching

103
00:09:32,228 --> 00:09:35,837
because that was the Surah(سورة) given to Rasool Allah ﷺ before he died.

104
00:09:36,384 --> 00:09:38,172
إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ وَالْفَتْحُ ۝

105
00:09:38,505 --> 00:09:42,059
وَرَأَيْتَ النَّاسَ يَدْخُلُونَ فِي دِينِ اللَّهِ أَفْوَاجًا ۝

106
00:09:42,344 --> 00:09:46,368
فَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَاسْتَغْفِرْهُ إِنَّهُ كَانَ تَوَّابًا۝

107
00:09:47,129 --> 00:09:54,227
So that means, this is my death and then with tears flowing down his cheeks.

108
00:09:55,201 --> 00:10:00,233
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: In the Name of Allah,

109
00:10:01,636 --> 00:10:04,565
I'm going to enjoin good and forbid evil.

110
00:10:05,464 --> 00:10:10,738
And I'm going to mobilize and prepare the soldiers to the enemies of Allah

111
00:10:11,107 --> 00:10:13,474
in the east and the west, of the Earth,

112
00:10:13,936 --> 00:10:19,747
until they say that Allah is One with no associates or until they pay me the Jizya(جزية)

113
00:10:19,975 --> 00:10:21,553
and they are humiliated.

114
00:10:21,998 --> 00:10:25,455
This is the command of Allah and this is the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Ullah.

115
00:10:25,670 --> 00:10:32,231
So when Allah takes away my soul, He would not find me weak or incapable

116
00:10:32,490 --> 00:10:36,230
and He will find me searching for the rewards of Al-Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

117
00:10:40,144 --> 00:10:46,246
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه has now made up his mind

118
00:10:47,363 --> 00:10:51,071
that they will start the Ghazoo(غزؤ) of Ar-Rome(ألروم).

119
00:10:51,262 --> 00:10:56,113
So, he calls the Sahabah(صحابه) to an assembly to meet

120
00:10:56,914 --> 00:10:59,780
and he will present them with his idea, Shura(شورى).

121
00:11:01,359 --> 00:11:05,159
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he invites, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

122
00:11:05,523 --> 00:11:08,362
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان), Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب),

123
00:11:08,463 --> 00:11:11,165
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف), Saad Ib Abi Waqas(سعدإبن أبي وقاص),

124
00:11:12,353 --> 00:11:15,369
Talha Bin Ubaid-Illah(طلحة بن عبيدالله), Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام)

125
00:11:15,846 --> 00:11:20,478
along with the leaders of Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) and Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

126
00:11:22,132 --> 00:11:27,825
And then Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه after praising Allah, He says that

127
00:11:28,787 --> 00:11:35,782
I am thinking about conquering Ash-Sham(ألشَّام), and fighting Ar-Rome(ألروم).

128
00:11:36,746 --> 00:11:41,209
So, that if someone dies, they die as a Shaheed(شَهِيد)

129
00:11:41,544 --> 00:11:46,767
and if they live, they live with victory and Ghanimah(غنيمه), booty.

130
00:11:49,484 --> 00:11:50,592
So what do you think?

131
00:11:50,786 --> 00:11:53,262
He is now seeking their advice.

132
00:11:54,257 --> 00:11:57,270
فَليُشِّرَ عَلَيَّ كُلُّ امْراٍ بمَبلَغ رَائ

133
00:11:58,065 --> 00:12:02,616
Give me your opinion? Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was the first to speak.

134
00:12:03,853 --> 00:12:09,251
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: He first of all said, after praising Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

135
00:12:09,772 --> 00:12:16,511
he said: Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gives His blessing to whomever He wishes.

136
00:12:18,077 --> 00:12:23,592
I have been thinking about this and I wanted to present the idea to you

137
00:12:23,992 --> 00:12:26,188
but here you are doing it before me.

138
00:12:27,006 --> 00:12:31,561
Because whenever we and you, race in anything good you always come out first.

139
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:35,217
And this is the favor of Allah that He gives to whomever He wishes.

140
00:12:36,209 --> 00:12:38,660
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying: I was thinking about the same thing.

141
00:12:39,315 --> 00:12:43,266
So this shows you that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

142
00:12:43,801 --> 00:12:46,770
were thinking seriously about the issue of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)

143
00:12:47,184 --> 00:12:50,865
and how to deal with it, and it has occupied their minds.

144
00:12:51,688 --> 00:12:54,335
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I was thinking about this

145
00:12:55,062 --> 00:12:57,641
and I never got around to doing it until

146
00:12:57,915 --> 00:13:00,243
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ destined that you would be the first one to mention.

147
00:13:00,438 --> 00:13:01,787
He said: My view is,

148
00:13:03,692 --> 00:13:06,790
 you send an army after an army into their land.

149
00:13:08,119 --> 00:13:09,399
The exact words,

150
00:13:10,166 --> 00:13:17,927
سَرِّبْ اِلَيْهِمْ بالْخيل في إثر الخيل وبعث الرجال تتبعو الرجال والجنود تتلوه الجنود

151
00:13:18,356 --> 00:13:24,777
Send in cavalries, following cavalries and infantries, following infantries,

152
00:13:25,035 --> 00:13:26,544
and armies following armies.

153
00:13:26,583 --> 00:13:28,532
What Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) means by that,

154
00:13:28,806 --> 00:13:36,085
is that you sent in the armies in batches, in pieces, one army after another

155
00:13:37,054 --> 00:13:43,899
and these armies attack from different directions and get into the land of Ar-Rome(ألروم).

156
00:13:44,173 --> 00:13:46,801
That was the view of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

157
00:13:48,563 --> 00:13:53,309
فان الله عزوجل ناصرٌ الدين ومعز الإسلام واهل

158
00:13:53,618 --> 00:13:57,276
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will give victory to His religion, and Allah will honor Islam.

159
00:13:57,753 --> 00:13:59,391
So this was the view of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

160
00:14:00,205 --> 00:14:02,514
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف), he stood up and said;

161
00:14:03,941 --> 00:14:07,752
I disagree with what Umar(عُمَر) said.

162
00:14:08,022 --> 00:14:10,784
This is Ar-Rome(ألروم), Wa Banul Asfar(وبنوالأصفر),

163
00:14:11,099 --> 00:14:14,623
Banul Asfar(بنوالأصفر) is the name the Arab used to give to the white, the European.

164
00:14:14,926 --> 00:14:19,207
They wouldn't call them white, they would say the yellow, Banul Asfar(بنوالأصفر).

165
00:14:19,649 --> 00:14:22,551
So the Romans are the sons of Al-Asfar(ألاصفر).

166
00:14:23,290 --> 00:14:25,213
حدٌ حديد ورُكنٌ الشديد

167
00:14:26,061 --> 00:14:28,655
They have a strong back.

168
00:14:29,361 --> 00:14:30,865
So Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) was saying

169
00:14:30,890 --> 00:14:35,154
that this is not an issue to be taken lightly, this is Ar-Rome(ألروم)

170
00:14:35,758 --> 00:14:41,863
and they have a very vast land and a lot of enforcements

171
00:14:42,972 --> 00:14:45,829
and whenever we get into their land,

172
00:14:46,004 --> 00:14:52,289
they will have an ocean of people behind that, to support them in their conflict with us.

173
00:14:52,693 --> 00:14:56,205
And that's a true characteristic of Ar-Rome(ألروم).

174
00:14:56,569 --> 00:15:01,249
It's an entire continent, and they were ruling in addition to the continent of Europe,

175
00:15:01,273 --> 00:15:05,286
they're ruling over North Africa, Egypt and Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

176
00:15:06,103 --> 00:15:09,017
So Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) was telling the Khalifah(خليفه) that

177
00:15:09,423 --> 00:15:11,960
this is not a regular foe, this is Ar-Rome(أللروم)!

178
00:15:12,408 --> 00:15:15,964
So he said: My view is to deal with the issue as following,

179
00:15:18,278 --> 00:15:22,764
والله ما أرى أن تقحم الخيل عليهم إقحامًا، ولكن تبعث الخيل،

180
00:15:22,931 --> 00:15:27,842
فتغير في أداني أرضهم، ثم تبعثها فتغير، ثم ترجع إليك

181
00:15:28,092 --> 00:15:32,358
فإذا فعلوا ذلك مرارًا أضروا بعدوهم، وغنموا من أداني أرضهم،

182
00:15:32,644 --> 00:15:34,324
فقووا بذلك على قتالهم

183
00:15:34,391 --> 00:15:42,327
My view is that you send in bands, of horsemen to raid their land

184
00:15:43,343 --> 00:15:47,262
and you raid the remote areas of their empire.

185
00:15:48,250 --> 00:15:53,636
So rather than sending conventional armies, you follow the way of raids

186
00:15:54,527 --> 00:16:00,541
small bands that would go in raid capture booty and come back.

187
00:16:01,183 --> 00:16:03,006
Now Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) was saying two things:

188
00:16:03,077 --> 00:16:08,329
First of all, you weaken them by doing that, so you always keep them on alert.

189
00:16:08,994 --> 00:16:13,021
And you always keep on hitting their defenses without giving them a chance to hit you back.

190
00:16:13,744 --> 00:16:17,659
 And then what Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) said and you can see

191
00:16:17,983 --> 00:16:23,419
that Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) is thinking, his mind was functioning in the business way.

192
00:16:24,209 --> 00:16:26,031
Yani(يعني) Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) was a businessman.

193
00:16:27,587 --> 00:16:30,271
So he's thinking about how to finance this campaign.

194
00:16:31,110 --> 00:16:36,430
He's saying these raids in addition to weakening the enemy and keeping them always on the defensive,

195
00:16:37,235 --> 00:16:39,947
through that booty, you would finance the campaign.

196
00:16:39,971 --> 00:16:43,913
 So, the treasury of the Islamic Khilafah(خِلَافَه) wouldn't have to pay for it.

197
00:16:44,994 --> 00:16:48,970
So rather than pay for it from Madina, you have them pay for their own campaign.

198
00:16:49,915 --> 00:16:54,855
And then when you are satisfied that's about time to make your move against them.

199
00:16:55,350 --> 00:17:02,177
Then what I want you to do or what I suggest you to do is that you send out messengers,

200
00:17:02,764 --> 00:17:05,957
to recruit the people of Yemen, from every corner

201
00:17:06,250 --> 00:17:08,379
and the people of Rabiya(ربيعة) and the people Mudhar(مضر).

202
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:14,282
And then you lead the army yourself or you appoint somebody to lead it in your place

203
00:17:14,688 --> 00:17:16,296
and In sha Allah(إن شاء الله), Allah will give you victory.

204
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:19,057
The opinion of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was an opinion,

205
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:22,186
you can see the influence of the personality in the opinion.

206
00:17:22,558 --> 00:17:24,791
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted an all out assault,

207
00:17:25,183 --> 00:17:30,020
send out the armies, let them fight them from every direction, until you take over the land.

208
00:17:30,497 --> 00:17:33,668
While Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) wanted to test the waters first.

209
00:17:34,661 --> 00:17:38,940
Go in send small bands, raid them, get booty.

210
00:17:39,752 --> 00:17:44,205
When you feel that you're ready to make your move and you you've tested the waters enough.

211
00:17:44,807 --> 00:17:48,049
Then you mobilize a huge army to do the effort for you.

212
00:17:49,311 --> 00:17:53,737
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) wants the Khalifah(خليفه) to invest a little bit in the beginning.

213
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:59,169
 If it's a profitable business, then put your money in it, but don't jump in it at once.

214
00:18:02,103 --> 00:18:05,391
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) then gave his opinion, he said;

215
00:18:06,235 --> 00:18:09,036
O Khalifah(خليفه) of the Messenger of Allah,

216
00:18:10,571 --> 00:18:16,312
Your opinion is blessed, so whatever you see befitting

217
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:19,241
go ahead with it and we will follow through.

218
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:22,969
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) is saying that we trust your opinion.

219
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:28,189
We trust your view, we trust your wisdom, you make the decision, and we'll follow you.

220
00:18:29,248 --> 00:18:32,360
Talha(طلحة), Zubair(زبير) and other Sahabah(صحابه) said the same thing.

221
00:18:32,673 --> 00:18:34,228
And Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) is quiet.

222
00:18:36,243 --> 00:18:39,812
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: We didn't hear from you, Ali(علي), how come you are quiet?

223
00:18:40,287 --> 00:18:41,908
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said;

224
00:18:43,343 --> 00:18:50,678
I think that you are a blessed person and you carry good omen

225
00:18:51,692 --> 00:18:57,209
and if you lead the army yourself or you appoint somebody in your place to do it,

226
00:18:57,639 --> 00:18:59,501
you will be victorious.

227
00:19:00,365 --> 00:19:03,941
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: How wonderful these words are.

228
00:19:04,106 --> 00:19:05,011
How do you know?

229
00:19:05,249 --> 00:19:07,344
Why did you make the judgment that I will win?

230
00:19:08,847 --> 00:19:12,363
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: I've heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say;

231
00:19:12,675 --> 00:19:19,761
لا يزال الدين ظاهرًا على كل من ناوأه، حتى يقوم الدين وأهله ظاهرين

232
00:19:20,867 --> 00:19:27,135
I've heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say that this religion will prevail against all the enemies

233
00:19:27,297 --> 00:19:32,526
until it stands up firm with the Muslims prevailing.

234
00:19:33,676 --> 00:19:36,123
This is a promise from Rasool Allah ﷺ it will happen.

235
00:19:37,254 --> 00:19:40,213
And this is the positiveness that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم had

236
00:19:40,491 --> 00:19:44,123
even before the battle they already knew the outcome, we're gonna win.

237
00:19:44,928 --> 00:19:46,639
It doesn't make a difference whether you led it

238
00:19:46,897 --> 00:19:50,417
or you appointed somebody in your place to lead it, which way you follow,

239
00:19:51,386 --> 00:19:52,952
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will give us victory.

240
00:19:53,939 --> 00:20:00,214
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was very happy to hear these words and he made up his mind

241
00:20:00,504 --> 00:20:03,293
and it was a mixture of both the opinion of Umar(عُمَر)

242
00:20:03,497 --> 00:20:05,173
and the opinion of Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف).

243
00:20:05,903 --> 00:20:08,388
What Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه did?

244
00:20:09,153 --> 00:20:15,576
Is that he sent out four armies and that's the part of the opinion of Umar(عُمَر) that he adopted.

245
00:20:15,793 --> 00:20:19,494
And then he followed the second part of the advice of Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن),

246
00:20:19,696 --> 00:20:25,203
and that is to mobilize people from every corner and bring them ahead to fight in this war.

247
00:20:25,477 --> 00:20:30,511
So he's bringing people, who are very far away from the battlefield,

248
00:20:31,583 --> 00:20:35,458
which means that there's an additional effort on their behalf.

249
00:20:35,483 --> 00:20:38,276
Because bringing the people of Rabiyah(ربيعة) from Iraq

250
00:20:38,314 --> 00:20:42,442
and the people of Yemen, from Al-Yemen(أليمن) and taking them all the way to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)

251
00:20:42,910 --> 00:20:44,335
is an additional effort.

252
00:20:44,970 --> 00:20:50,819
But since this is a confrontation with the superpower of the time,

253
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:56,006
and it is to wrestle their control over the holy land which they view as the Heartland,

254
00:20:56,843 --> 00:21:01,180
this is not going to be an easy affair and therefore it needs some special recruitment effort.

255
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:07,689
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه send Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) with a letter to Yemen.

256
00:21:08,792 --> 00:21:10,098
This letter states,

257
00:21:11,077 --> 00:21:13,918
In the Name of Allah, the all Compassionate, the Merciful,

258
00:21:14,674 --> 00:21:19,974
from the successor of the Messenger of Allah, to whomever this message is read to,

259
00:21:20,127 --> 00:21:23,580
from the believers and the Muslims of the people of Yemen.

260
00:21:23,837 --> 00:21:24,992
(سلامٌ عليكم).

261
00:21:26,042 --> 00:21:28,605
Allah has prescribed Jihad(جهاد) on the believers

262
00:21:28,738 --> 00:21:31,861
and commanded them to set out light and heavy.

263
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:37,699
Allah سبحانه وتعالى said fight in the path of Allah with your wealth and yourselves.

264
00:21:38,854 --> 00:21:42,509
Jihad(جهاد) is a mandate and its reward from Allah is great.

265
00:21:43,514 --> 00:21:47,764
We have assembled the Muslims in our area for Jihad(جهاد) against the Romans in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)

266
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:49,816
 and they hasten towards that.

267
00:21:50,334 --> 00:21:56,056
Their armies have already set out, so hasten towards, what they have hasten towards,

268
00:21:56,641 --> 00:22:01,861
you would then get one of the best two, either martyrdom, or victory and booty.

269
00:22:02,578 --> 00:22:05,627
Allah is not pleased by words alone without deeds.

270
00:22:05,897 --> 00:22:12,305
So Jihad(جهاد) must continue until they follow the religion of truth and accept the governance of the book of Allah.

271
00:22:12,893 --> 00:22:17,217
May Allah protect your religion, guide your hearts, purify your deeds,

272
00:22:17,499 --> 00:22:19,995
and grant you the reward of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

273
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:25,443
In this letter, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) is telling the people the objectives

274
00:22:25,576 --> 00:22:28,499
of fighting in the sake of Allah, which are two.

275
00:22:28,936 --> 00:22:29,957
Number one;

276
00:22:31,155 --> 00:22:36,350
that this is part of the Ibadah(عبادة) regardless, it is part of the Ibadah(عبادة).

277
00:22:37,530 --> 00:22:41,628
He said that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ does not accept words without deeds.

278
00:22:42,001 --> 00:22:44,891
So for your words, to be true,

279
00:22:45,664 --> 00:22:48,146
they must be accompanied by Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

280
00:22:48,712 --> 00:22:53,620
The second objective is that people either become Muslim or they give the Jizya(جزية)

281
00:22:53,816 --> 00:22:56,916
and they accept the rule of the book of Allah because by giving Jizya(جزية),

282
00:22:57,512 --> 00:22:59,992
they have accepted the Hukum(حكم) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ in Qur'an

283
00:23:00,074 --> 00:23:02,425
because Jizya(جزية) is a Quranic command.

284
00:23:03,170 --> 00:23:06,541
So these are the two objectives of fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

285
00:23:07,326 --> 00:23:11,698
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) would go and read this letter to the people in every town.

286
00:23:11,943 --> 00:23:15,022
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) came back to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

287
00:23:15,046 --> 00:23:16,670
giving him the good news, he said;

288
00:23:16,776 --> 00:23:19,278
أبشر قد عطوك شعثًا غبرا

289
00:23:19,524 --> 00:23:22,463
ابطال اليمن وشجعانها وفرسانها

290
00:23:22,725 --> 00:23:26,772
وقد سارو اليك بضرار والحرم والأموال

291
00:23:27,685 --> 00:23:31,712
He said: Rejoice! They have came to you covered in dust,

292
00:23:32,270 --> 00:23:36,694
the heroes of Yemen and the brave men among them and their knights.

293
00:23:37,038 --> 00:23:41,594
They came to you along with their children, their wives and their wealth.

294
00:23:42,207 --> 00:23:46,685
So this is a campaign that demands them to move out of their land

295
00:23:46,974 --> 00:23:50,458
because of the huge distance so they are moving out

296
00:23:50,747 --> 00:23:54,212
with their wealth and with their families, going Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

297
00:23:54,865 --> 00:24:00,213
So this is the level of sacrifice that was demanded in those days.

298
00:24:02,321 --> 00:24:06,653
One of the kings of Yemen, his name is Zulkulaa Al-Himyari(ذوالكلاع ألحميري).

299
00:24:08,003 --> 00:24:14,461
He came into Madina, five days after Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) arrived, immediate response.

300
00:24:15,690 --> 00:24:18,488
Came in with a few 100 of his followers.

301
00:24:19,179 --> 00:24:31,122
He came in, wearing a crown all of these jewels in it and dressed in a robe with gold, very extravagant.

302
00:24:31,395 --> 00:24:37,612
He's a King, comes into Madina and he sees the Khalifah(خليفه) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

303
00:24:38,208 --> 00:24:44,405
wrapped in very mediocre and normal pieces of cloth,

304
00:24:45,890 --> 00:24:50,292
without any bodyguards, living in a mud house.

305
00:24:52,367 --> 00:24:56,783
That sight of the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims affected this man so much.

306
00:24:57,479 --> 00:25:03,176
He took off all of those expensive clothes, went to the market of Madina

307
00:25:03,793 --> 00:25:08,148
where all what you would find is very rough fabrics.

308
00:25:08,668 --> 00:25:11,351
He bought himself some of that and he put it on.

309
00:25:12,012 --> 00:25:16,007
His people told him you're gonna embarrass us in front of Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) Wal-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار),

310
00:25:16,761 --> 00:25:19,659
 he said that's it, that's what that way is over.

311
00:25:20,053 --> 00:25:22,418
And now we're gonna follow the way of Zuhd(زهد), austerity.

312
00:25:24,485 --> 00:25:29,720
When people see a role model in front of them, it is more powerful than words

313
00:25:30,406 --> 00:25:35,301
you could have spoken to Zulkulaa Al-Himyari(ذوالكلاع ألحميري) about Zuhd(زهد) in a theoretical way,

314
00:25:35,563 --> 00:25:37,856
 it wouldn't have that impact on him.

315
00:25:38,650 --> 00:25:41,105
That the sight of the Khalifah(خليفه) Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had.

316
00:25:42,612 --> 00:25:48,164
Also people usually follow the person, who's in power, and the nation who's in power

317
00:25:48,683 --> 00:25:53,222
 people usually follow the role model of the powerful nations,

318
00:25:53,841 --> 00:25:56,825
their way becomes the adopted way.

319
00:25:57,552 --> 00:26:03,675
So people listen to their songs, watch their movies, wear their clothes,

320
00:26:04,464 --> 00:26:08,496
and that is something that Ibn Khaldoon(إبن خلدون) said, is a human trait

321
00:26:09,402 --> 00:26:12,269
the weak follows the strong.

322
00:26:14,269 --> 00:26:19,097
Zulkulaa Al-Himyari(ذوالكلاع ألحميري) who's a king, but he's under the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) now.

323
00:26:19,593 --> 00:26:26,390
When he sees that the Khalifah(خليفه) doesn't mind wearing very cheap clothes, rough fabrics.

324
00:26:27,420 --> 00:26:32,279
He was willing to take off all of that extravagant luxurious clothes that he had on,

325
00:26:33,017 --> 00:26:37,080
because now their role model was Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

326
00:26:39,055 --> 00:26:41,764
So the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were setting new standards

327
00:26:42,852 --> 00:26:45,003
and they were giving the people a new example.

328
00:26:46,182 --> 00:26:49,393
So without them speaking, they would go into these territories

329
00:26:49,735 --> 00:26:51,366
because they opened them with Izzah(عزة).

330
00:26:51,976 --> 00:26:56,122
See they didn't go into make Da'wah(دعوة) in a very humiliating way.

331
00:26:56,508 --> 00:26:58,891
They didn't go begging the people to become Muslim

332
00:26:59,974 --> 00:27:03,062
and compromising in the religion, they went in with Izzah(عزة).

333
00:27:03,545 --> 00:27:07,065
They went in with armies, and they conquered the lands of people.

334
00:27:07,561 --> 00:27:10,972
And then they would go to the Masjid(مسجد) and the people would come to them to learn from them.

335
00:27:11,540 --> 00:27:15,821
Because they would see them as the people, whom the example of, should be followed.

336
00:27:16,171 --> 00:27:20,393
So the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم without speaking, people would adopt their ways.

337
00:27:22,213 --> 00:27:25,994
And with little effort, entire tribes will enter into the fold of Islam.

338
00:27:27,477 --> 00:27:30,256
So the method of Da'wah(دعوة) of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

339
00:27:30,725 --> 00:27:35,091
was a way where they would present Islam in a very honorable way, with Izzah(عزة).

340
00:27:37,873 --> 00:27:45,238
So now, Al-Khalifah رضي الله عنه set the armies, four armies.

341
00:27:46,159 --> 00:27:49,842
First Army was the army of Yazeed Bin Abi Sufiyan(يزيد بن أبي سفيان).

342
00:27:50,088 --> 00:27:57,473
He appointed him over 7000 soldiers and his destination was Dimashq(دمشق), Damascus.

343
00:27:58,342 --> 00:28:01,747
Second Army under the leadership of Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة)

344
00:28:02,890 --> 00:28:05,834
with 3000 Soldiers, his destination is Tabook(تبوك)

345
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:08,736
 and to protect the rear of the Muslims

346
00:28:09,327 --> 00:28:14,434
and to be a reinforcement for them because the Tabook(تبوك) is the closest towards Al-Madina.

347
00:28:15,085 --> 00:28:19,753
Third Army 3000 led by Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(ابوعبيدة عمرو بن جراح)

348
00:28:19,777 --> 00:28:22,041
and his destination is Hims(حمص) in Syria.

349
00:28:22,963 --> 00:28:27,137
The Fourth Army of 7000, led by Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص)

350
00:28:27,298 --> 00:28:31,480
and his destination was Falastine(فلسطين) and he sent them out.

351
00:28:32,107 --> 00:28:36,589
Al-Khalifah(ألخليفه) would walk with every one of these leaders,

352
00:28:36,873 --> 00:28:41,532
while they are riding their horses and the Khalifah(خليفه) is walking

353
00:28:41,883 --> 00:28:45,765
and he would give them a Naseeha(نصيحة), give every one of them an advice.

354
00:28:45,984 --> 00:28:49,675
I'll read to you the advice that he gave to Yazeed Ibn Abi Sufiyan(يزيد إبن أبي سفيان)

355
00:28:49,700 --> 00:28:52,718
which was the first army to march, to set out.

356
00:28:53,855 --> 00:28:58,711
He said: I am appointing you to lead this army to test you and to try you.

357
00:28:58,906 --> 00:29:02,433
If you perform well, I will give you more.

358
00:29:03,012 --> 00:29:05,005
And if you don't, I will change you.

359
00:29:05,509 --> 00:29:07,649
So I advise you to have Taqwa(تقوى) of Allah

360
00:29:08,102 --> 00:29:12,355
because he can see your inside just as he can see your outside.

361
00:29:13,423 --> 00:29:17,296
I'm appointing you into the post of Khalid Bin Saeed Bin Aas(خالد بن سعيد بن ألعاص).

362
00:29:17,893 --> 00:29:20,967
Stay away from the arrogance and tribalism of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة),

363
00:29:21,174 --> 00:29:24,790
when you join your soldiers, be a good companion of them.

364
00:29:24,847 --> 00:29:29,675
And if you deliver a speech to them, then be brief, otherwise they will forget the message.

365
00:29:30,393 --> 00:29:35,113
Improve the state of yourself, the state of your soldiers will improve.

366
00:29:35,975 --> 00:29:37,920
Pray Salah(صلاة) at the appointed time

367
00:29:38,217 --> 00:29:42,161
and complete your Sujood(سجود) and Rukooh(ركوع) and have Khushoo(خشوع) in Salah(صلاة).

368
00:29:43,259 --> 00:29:47,627
When you receive envoys from your enemy, be kind with them and generous,

369
00:29:47,993 --> 00:29:53,185
but do not allow them extended stay, otherwise they will learn of your weaknesses.

370
00:29:53,728 --> 00:29:58,738
Have them stay among your strongest forces and allow no one but yourself to speak to them.

371
00:30:00,244 --> 00:30:03,109
When you seek counsel, be straightforward and truthful,

372
00:30:03,361 --> 00:30:05,280
in order to receive the best advice.

373
00:30:05,958 --> 00:30:08,852
Spend time at night chatting with your soldiers,

374
00:30:09,312 --> 00:30:13,428
then you will receive news and veils will be lifted,

375
00:30:14,052 --> 00:30:17,679
spread out your guards and pay them unannounced visits

376
00:30:18,100 --> 00:30:22,939
and whenever you see any carelessness in guarding your army, then punish them moderately.

377
00:30:23,565 --> 00:30:25,885
Do not spend time with people, who waste their time,

378
00:30:26,272 --> 00:30:28,491
but spend it with the people of truth and loyalty.

379
00:30:29,409 --> 00:30:34,804
Beware of financial abuse because it draws poverty closer and victory further.

380
00:30:35,651 --> 00:30:39,251
You will find men devoted to worship in monasteries, leave them alone.

381
00:30:41,545 --> 00:30:46,045
This is a wonderful advice that Al-Khalifah(ألخليفه) gave to Yazeed(يزيد),

382
00:30:46,559 --> 00:30:50,097
we want to take a look at some of the lessons to be learned from it.

383
00:30:50,523 --> 00:30:53,226
Number one, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) saying that

384
00:30:53,639 --> 00:30:56,401
being a leader you're going to be held accountable for what you're doing.

385
00:30:57,378 --> 00:30:59,705
He said: I put you in this position to try you.

386
00:30:59,726 --> 00:31:03,885
This is the first time he's appointed Yazeed(يزيد) to a position of leadership. He said:

387
00:31:04,378 --> 00:31:07,527
I'm putting you in this position to test you and try you.

388
00:31:08,042 --> 00:31:10,857
If you perform well, I'll give you more.

389
00:31:11,008 --> 00:31:14,599
If not I will change you, this is not for life.

390
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:19,102
When the leader feels that their appointment is for life, they would slack,

391
00:31:19,930 --> 00:31:25,382
so Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is saying you could be changed depending on how you conduct yourself

392
00:31:26,583 --> 00:31:30,422
and you are going to be held accountable for everything that you do.

393
00:31:31,625 --> 00:31:33,250
Number two, the Taqwa(تقوى) of Allah.

394
00:31:34,201 --> 00:31:37,327
This is the most important Naseeha(نصيحة) to fear Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

395
00:31:37,952 --> 00:31:41,237
Number three, he is warning him the perils of nationalism and tribalism.

396
00:31:42,452 --> 00:31:46,897
Now Yazeed Ibn Abi Sufiyan(يزيد إبن أبي سفيان) comes from a very prominent family in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

397
00:31:47,296 --> 00:31:49,479
his father Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) was the leader of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

398
00:31:49,804 --> 00:31:54,612
and he's the one, who led the war against Muhammadﷺ for the major part of his life.

399
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:57,841
But then Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) became Muslim when Makkah was opened.

400
00:31:58,073 --> 00:32:01,711
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is now appointing his son Yazeed(يزيد) to lead an army.

401
00:32:01,893 --> 00:32:08,069
So he's warning him from any remnants of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة) that might still be in the heart of the new Muslim.

402
00:32:08,784 --> 00:32:10,937
 Stay away from tribalism and nationalism!

403
00:32:11,615 --> 00:32:13,390
Now it's the brotherhood of Islam.

404
00:32:15,961 --> 00:32:18,273
He said: Be brief.

405
00:32:18,804 --> 00:32:23,179
 When you speak to your soldiers, don't give them long reminders and this is a Naseeha(نصيحة)

406
00:32:23,204 --> 00:32:27,367
that should to be given to every speaker, don't give their long reminders because,

407
00:32:27,392 --> 00:32:28,972
يُنسي آخرالكلام أوَّلًا

408
00:32:29,501 --> 00:32:32,118
The latter part will make you forget the former.

409
00:32:32,595 --> 00:32:36,985
So be brief, especially when you're delivering to them instructions of battle,

410
00:32:37,290 --> 00:32:41,434
Be very brief if you want your words to be remembered, and then he said;

411
00:32:42,219 --> 00:32:44,559
Take care of yourself first.

412
00:32:44,856 --> 00:32:54,050
As the Khalifah(خليفه) he is teaching the leaders that if you want your soldiers to improve,

413
00:32:54,425 --> 00:32:55,981
then you need to improve yourself.

414
00:32:56,425 --> 00:32:58,719
If you have Taqwa(تقوى), they will have Taqwa(تقوى),

415
00:32:58,971 --> 00:33:02,284
if you take care of the commands of Allah, they will take care of the commands of Allah

416
00:33:03,148 --> 00:33:06,643
if you observe the orders of Allah, they will observe them too.

417
00:33:06,890 --> 00:33:11,634
So when the leader improves himself, that improvement is actually an investment for the people

418
00:33:11,992 --> 00:33:13,133
 it will improve them too.

419
00:33:14,090 --> 00:33:16,509
You can't expect the people to be truthful when you're not.

420
00:33:16,834 --> 00:33:19,595
You can't expect them to be honest, when you're not honest with them.

421
00:33:20,467 --> 00:33:23,994
You can't expect them to sacrifice when the leader is not sacrificing.

422
00:33:24,482 --> 00:33:27,289
But when the people see all of these virtues in the leader

423
00:33:27,664 --> 00:33:29,266
that will encourage them to do the same.

424
00:33:31,930 --> 00:33:34,204
Number six, the importance of Salah(صلاة).

425
00:33:35,789 --> 00:33:38,559
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is sending out an army to fight an enemy.

426
00:33:39,332 --> 00:33:42,412
You couldn't be busy with preparing the logistics of the army

427
00:33:42,591 --> 00:33:44,174
that did not make him forget Salah(صلاة).

428
00:33:44,254 --> 00:33:48,775
In fact, he would not forget Salah(صلاة) and he would insist on the importance of it

429
00:33:48,855 --> 00:33:52,060
because he knows that victory comes through our Ibadah(عبادة).

430
00:33:52,772 --> 00:33:55,625
So he's telling him that you need to pray Salah(صلاة) on time.

431
00:33:56,437 --> 00:33:59,737
The Rukoo(ركوع) and Sujood(سجود) needs to be complete.

432
00:34:00,549 --> 00:34:03,900
Because in army you're moving from one place to another you're busy.

433
00:34:04,228 --> 00:34:10,551
You're in a state of fear, that's not an excuse to make you pray the Salah(صلاة) without Khushoo(خشوع).

434
00:34:10,912 --> 00:34:13,324
You still have to have Khushoo(خشوع) in your Salah(صلاة),

435
00:34:13,515 --> 00:34:17,947
even though there are as many distractions, as there could be,

436
00:34:18,612 --> 00:34:21,190
there is no situation with more distractions

437
00:34:21,534 --> 00:34:23,119
than an army fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

438
00:34:23,565 --> 00:34:25,569
Nevertheless, you still have to have Khushoo(خشوع)

439
00:34:25,710 --> 00:34:27,424
and Rukoo(ركوع) and Sujood(سجود) need to be complete.

440
00:34:27,448 --> 00:34:32,427
What about the people who are living in the luxury with no problems whatsoever,

441
00:34:32,452 --> 00:34:37,000
no distractions whatsoever, and their Salah(صلاة) is like an exercise, pushups.

442
00:34:37,830 --> 00:34:43,209
Number seven, kindness and care towards the envoys of the enemy.

443
00:34:43,233 --> 00:34:48,383
He said: When you receive messengers, or envoys or delegations coming from the enemy,

444
00:34:48,590 --> 00:34:52,070
be kind with them even though they are your enemy, but Be kind.

445
00:34:52,770 --> 00:34:56,848
Be generous with them when they come and don't allow them to stay for too long,

446
00:34:57,379 --> 00:34:59,393
generous is something, kind is something

447
00:34:59,577 --> 00:35:02,492
and allowing them free access to your army is something else.

448
00:35:04,155 --> 00:35:06,857
So kindness is not being naive.

449
00:35:07,135 --> 00:35:10,469
So he said: Don't allow them to stay for so long.

450
00:35:10,627 --> 00:35:18,441
And then he told him and have them stay among the strongest and more powerful forces that you have.

451
00:35:18,790 --> 00:35:22,961
So, that they get an impression of your strength and not your weakness.

452
00:35:23,997 --> 00:35:26,346
And then he said: Don't allow anybody speak to them.

453
00:35:26,754 --> 00:35:30,136
You alone should speak to these envoys.

454
00:35:31,508 --> 00:35:35,024
Number eight, Shura(شورى) only works with honesty and truth.

455
00:35:35,148 --> 00:35:41,096
When you are seeking Shura(شورى) from your council of generals or leaders of the army.

456
00:35:41,828 --> 00:35:46,523
You have to give them a complete picture of what is happening,

457
00:35:46,548 --> 00:35:49,005
if you want to get the right advice

458
00:35:49,523 --> 00:35:53,088
you can't give them some information and withhold some

459
00:35:53,327 --> 00:35:55,445
and then think that you're going to get the right Naseeha(نصيحة).

460
00:35:56,077 --> 00:35:58,414
If you are asking for Shura(شورى).

461
00:35:58,819 --> 00:36:02,041
The person who's giving you Shura(شورى) must have all of the variables

462
00:36:02,081 --> 00:36:04,716
in order to make a judgment and give you the right Naseeha(نصيحة).

463
00:36:05,556 --> 00:36:09,501
Because you might say well, Allah سبحانه وتعالى has said that if you make Shura(شورى),

464
00:36:09,633 --> 00:36:12,695
your decision will be right and I made Shura(شورى) and it didn't turn out to be right.

465
00:36:12,719 --> 00:36:17,100
That's because he didn't tell the people the entire story.

466
00:36:18,361 --> 00:36:22,441
So Naseeha(نصيحة) needs to be done in the right way, if you want the fruits of Naseeha(نصيحة).

467
00:36:23,734 --> 00:36:28,053
Number nine, intermingling with the soldiers, you should not be aloof from the soldiers.

468
00:36:28,078 --> 00:36:29,762
He said: Go and chat with them at night.

469
00:36:30,593 --> 00:36:36,534
And night time is the time, when you would get the information and the news

470
00:36:36,713 --> 00:36:40,476
because that's when the Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) there's something about talking at night.

471
00:36:40,964 --> 00:36:48,212
The resistance is less, so a person is more willing to speak about private things or secrets

472
00:36:48,673 --> 00:36:52,873
that otherwise they wouldn't be willing to speak about during daytime

473
00:36:53,993 --> 00:36:58,041
if you want to discover something investigate it at night.

474
00:37:00,444 --> 00:37:03,389
Something about the moonlight and the stars

475
00:37:04,389 --> 00:37:09,118
romantic settings that makes a person very open in their talk.

476
00:37:10,167 --> 00:37:14,257
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم had Hikmah(حكمة) and wisdom they knew how to get things done.

477
00:37:14,487 --> 00:37:18,127
So he said: Go and chat with your soldiers at night, the veils will be lifted.

478
00:37:19,396 --> 00:37:22,432
You'll get to know the reality of the condition of your soldiers.

479
00:37:22,912 --> 00:37:25,833
That's how you will have access to information and news.

480
00:37:26,419 --> 00:37:28,657
Go around! Spend time with them! Talk!

481
00:37:31,009 --> 00:37:33,884
Number Ten, guarding the Muslim army.

482
00:37:34,504 --> 00:37:38,859
He said: Appoint guards and then pay them unannounced visits.

483
00:37:40,434 --> 00:37:44,821
And if you see any flaws, any mistakes then you need to punish them for it,

484
00:37:44,845 --> 00:37:46,710
but punish them for it modestly.

485
00:37:47,313 --> 00:37:48,559
Don't be extreme.

486
00:37:49,662 --> 00:37:55,047
Don't give them free go at everything but at the same time don't be very strict.

487
00:37:56,282 --> 00:37:58,345
Number 11, the importance of good company.

488
00:37:58,376 --> 00:38:00,818
Don't spend your time with people, who waste their time.

489
00:38:01,557 --> 00:38:05,467
You need to be serious surround yourself with the people of As-Sidq(ألصدق),

490
00:38:05,568 --> 00:38:07,350
the people of Al-Haq(ألحق), the people have the truth

491
00:38:07,678 --> 00:38:09,612
and Ahlul Wafaa(أهل الوفاء), the people who are grateful.

492
00:38:10,624 --> 00:38:14,248
You want to have grateful people around you, people who will help you,

493
00:38:14,855 --> 00:38:18,604
when you're in need, people who will not betray you in times of difficulty.

494
00:38:19,191 --> 00:38:21,758
Because there are some people who are very good in amusing.

495
00:38:22,464 --> 00:38:25,486
They could make a very good company to amuse you.

496
00:38:26,607 --> 00:38:30,567
But when things get serious, they're gonna flee from around you.

497
00:38:30,794 --> 00:38:32,902
So he said: Have the people of Wafa(وفا) around you.

498
00:38:33,614 --> 00:38:36,838
As a soldier, you want to have loyal people around you.

499
00:38:37,173 --> 00:38:42,145
So he is saying to the leader of the Army, have these as your close associates.

500
00:38:43,213 --> 00:38:45,693
Number 12, the handling of money.

501
00:38:46,260 --> 00:38:50,053
He said: If there is financial abuse in the army, Ghalool(غلول).

502
00:38:50,903 --> 00:38:57,060
This would make poverty closer to you and victory further away.

503
00:38:58,059 --> 00:39:01,531
When Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة) was setting out the Khalifah(خليفه) accompanied him

504
00:39:01,931 --> 00:39:05,712
and then he asked him, he said: Did you hear my instructions to Yazeed(يزيد)?

505
00:39:06,095 --> 00:39:09,072
He said: Yes! He said: Follow them.

506
00:39:09,782 --> 00:39:12,870
And there are a few more points which I forgot to mention to him

507
00:39:13,191 --> 00:39:14,501
and I will mention them to you.

508
00:39:14,930 --> 00:39:18,017
He said: Be patient when you meet your enemy.

509
00:39:19,152 --> 00:39:20,168
Patience is the key.

510
00:39:20,777 --> 00:39:23,019
صْبِرُواْ وَصَابِرُواْ وَرَابِطُواْ

511
00:39:23,558 --> 00:39:26,222
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: Isbiroo(إصبرو) be patient, Wasabiroo(وصابرو),

512
00:39:26,558 --> 00:39:29,792
Wasabiroo(وصابرو) means is that you outdo the enemy in patience.

513
00:39:30,394 --> 00:39:34,354
So you could be patient, but the enemy could be more patient than you.

514
00:39:34,421 --> 00:39:37,767
I mean, you could be following the first part of the Ayah(آية) which is, Isbiroo(إصبرو), Be patient.

515
00:39:38,115 --> 00:39:41,270
But what if your enemy is also patient, What do you do? Sabiro(صابرو)

516
00:39:41,732 --> 00:39:46,617
which means you compete with them in the degree of patience, until you outdo them in that.

517
00:39:47,421 --> 00:39:53,382
And there's a story about Antara(أنترى), who's like a legendary figure in courage and bravery.

518
00:39:54,377 --> 00:39:59,322
Antara(أنترى) was asked by someone how come you always win against your enemy?

519
00:39:59,393 --> 00:40:01,424
What makes you always victorious?

520
00:40:02,658 --> 00:40:05,695
He said: I'll tell you, why? You stick your finger in my mouth.

521
00:40:06,546 --> 00:40:09,999
And I'll stick my finger in yours and then we'll both bite.

522
00:40:11,476 --> 00:40:14,270
He said: Alright! Let's try this and he put his finger

523
00:40:14,780 --> 00:40:18,341
so Antara(عنترى) started biting his finger and the other guy is biting Antara(عنترى)'s finger

524
00:40:19,073 --> 00:40:22,230
and they're crushing each others finger.

525
00:40:22,925 --> 00:40:25,709
So the man after a while, he screams and said: I give up.

526
00:40:26,170 --> 00:40:27,227
Antara(عنترى) said;

527
00:40:27,818 --> 00:40:32,542
If you would have waited for just one more moment, I would have given up

528
00:40:33,147 --> 00:40:34,930
and that's why I always win against my enemy.

529
00:40:36,451 --> 00:40:40,163
So it's that one moment that you are willing to wait

530
00:40:40,392 --> 00:40:44,320
to outdo the enemy in patients that makes it or breaks it.

531
00:40:46,579 --> 00:40:51,607
Second Naseeha(نَصيحة), visit the sick and the injured and attend the Janazah(جنازة),

532
00:40:52,269 --> 00:40:54,107
the leader must be part of the people.

533
00:40:54,607 --> 00:40:56,491
When a soldier is injured, visit them.

534
00:40:56,847 --> 00:41:01,782
When a soldier is sick visit them, when there is a Janazah(جناز), attend the Janazah(جنازة).

535
00:41:02,649 --> 00:41:06,522
Don't be separate from the people, don't make a barrier between you and them.

536
00:41:08,679 --> 00:41:11,370
And then he said: Remember Allah a lot,

537
00:41:11,797 --> 00:41:13,834
وَذْكُرالله كَثِيْرَا

538
00:41:13,894 --> 00:41:15,271
"Remember Allah a lot. "

539
00:41:15,773 --> 00:41:20,265
So, these are his words of advice that he gave to Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة).

540
00:41:20,734 --> 00:41:23,439
He also gives them a words to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), but before.

541
00:41:23,996 --> 00:41:26,613
With Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was appointed to Oman(عمان).

542
00:41:27,175 --> 00:41:31,298
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ to be the governor of Oman(عمان).

543
00:41:31,750 --> 00:41:32,925
 When the Riddah(ردَّة) happened.

544
00:41:33,214 --> 00:41:37,131
He had to move out - but then Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) sent him a letter saying;

545
00:41:38,364 --> 00:41:42,520
I have restored you to the office to which the Messenger of Allah appointed you,

546
00:41:42,763 --> 00:41:43,608
meaning Oman(عمان).

547
00:41:44,101 --> 00:41:48,145
 I would like Abu Abdullah(أبوعبدالله) to devote you entirely

548
00:41:48,234 --> 00:41:52,967
to that which is better for you in your present life and in the hereafter,

549
00:41:53,127 --> 00:41:55,740
unless that which you have now is preferable to you.

550
00:41:56,049 --> 00:41:56,900
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is saying,

551
00:41:57,994 --> 00:42:01,414
Rasool Ullah appointed you to Oman(عمان), I will appoint you to the same post.

552
00:42:01,674 --> 00:42:05,047
However, I have something which is better for you in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

553
00:42:05,300 --> 00:42:06,502
and better for you in Aakhira(آخرة).

554
00:42:06,815 --> 00:42:13,784
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) did not want to change the post of anyone, who was appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

555
00:42:14,030 --> 00:42:15,516
unless he's going to give him something better.

556
00:42:16,151 --> 00:42:19,665
He never ever fired anybody who was appointed by Rasool Ullah.

557
00:42:20,150 --> 00:42:23,688
So, since Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was appointed by Rasool Ullah, to govern Oman(عمان),

558
00:42:23,993 --> 00:42:26,310
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: I'm giving you that appointment again.

559
00:42:26,390 --> 00:42:29,305
However, there's something better I'm going to leave the choice to you.

560
00:42:30,454 --> 00:42:34,636
And what Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had in mind is the opening of Falastine(فلسطين),

561
00:42:36,183 --> 00:42:38,738
which was better for Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

562
00:42:38,763 --> 00:42:43,786
because it's the position of Jihad(جهاد) first of all, and it's better for him in Akhirah(آخرة).

563
00:42:45,157 --> 00:42:50,927
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) sent a letter back he said: I am one of the arrows of Islam

564
00:42:51,305 --> 00:42:55,467
and you after Allah are the one, who shoots them and collect them.

565
00:42:55,846 --> 00:42:59,018
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) is saying: I'm an arrow that belongs to Islam,

566
00:42:59,768 --> 00:43:01,006
and you are the archer.

567
00:43:01,901 --> 00:43:06,456
Look for the strongest, most fearsome and best of them and aim me at it

568
00:43:06,981 --> 00:43:08,055
and I will be your soldier.

569
00:43:08,897 --> 00:43:14,209
I am an arrow you point it to whichever direction you want and aim me

570
00:43:14,660 --> 00:43:15,602
and I will be your soldier.

571
00:43:16,429 --> 00:43:20,084
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) immediately called him to come, summoned him to come to Madina,

572
00:43:20,471 --> 00:43:23,644
 and he appointed him to lead the army that's going to Falastine(فلسطين).

573
00:43:25,179 --> 00:43:30,436
Now, the four armies took separate routes into Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)

574
00:43:31,643 --> 00:43:37,346
and Heracul(هراقل) sensing the danger has set base in Antaqia(أنتاكية), Antioch.

575
00:43:38,330 --> 00:43:42,712
And he in turn, arranged his armies

576
00:43:44,022 --> 00:43:49,218
and he sent out four armies to descend on the four armies of the Sahabah(صحابه).

577
00:43:50,267 --> 00:43:53,210
The first army led by his brother, Theodore

578
00:43:54,400 --> 00:43:59,562
90,000 soldiers, and they are to meet Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

579
00:43:59,774 --> 00:44:01,491
Now Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) how many did he have?

580
00:44:01,673 --> 00:44:02,578
7000,

581
00:44:02,975 --> 00:44:05,036
7000 against 90,000.

582
00:44:05,480 --> 00:44:09,272
George the son of Theodore is to meet with Yazeed(يزيد), it doesn't mention the numbers.

583
00:44:09,660 --> 00:44:12,754
Darqus to Sharhabil(شرحبيل) also doesn't mention the numbers

584
00:44:13,015 --> 00:44:19,599
and Qabqar in Latin, it's Visorious it's 60,000 to meet Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح).

585
00:44:19,666 --> 00:44:21,791
So these are huge armies.

586
00:44:22,196 --> 00:44:30,150
Now, when the Sahabah(صحابه) the leaders of the four armies saw the numbers that they are facing,

587
00:44:30,809 --> 00:44:33,570
 they started sending letters to the Khalifah(خليفه), help us.

588
00:44:34,802 --> 00:44:37,132
Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) sent a letter. Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) sent a letter.

589
00:44:37,189 --> 00:44:39,219
Yazeed(يزيد) they're all asking for help.

590
00:44:41,288 --> 00:44:44,060
Allah Ho Alam(ألله أغلم) maybe they didn't expect such numbers or what?

591
00:44:44,081 --> 00:44:50,479
But Al-Khalifah(ألخليفه) was starting to get all of these S.O.S. messages from the generals in the field.

592
00:44:51,299 --> 00:44:52,846
Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) he sent a letter, he said:

593
00:44:52,867 --> 00:44:55,372
In the Name of Allah, the all Compassionate, the Merciful.

594
00:44:55,435 --> 00:45:00,450
To the servant of Allah Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), the successor of the messenger of Allah ﷺ

595
00:45:00,687 --> 00:45:02,490
 from Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح)

596
00:45:02,511 --> 00:45:03,416
(السلام عليكم)

597
00:45:03,773 --> 00:45:08,724
I praise Allah and I ask Allah to honor Islam and his followers and to grant them victory.

598
00:45:09,660 --> 00:45:14,120
I have received news that Heraclius the king of the Romans

599
00:45:14,515 --> 00:45:18,401
has set base in a town in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) called; Antioch

600
00:45:18,820 --> 00:45:24,377
and that he sent out to his people, the people of his kingdom and He mobilized them.

601
00:45:24,962 --> 00:45:27,890
They responded to his call in great numbers.

602
00:45:28,271 --> 00:45:31,790
I wanted to inform you of this to give us your opinion.

603
00:45:32,033 --> 00:45:34,580
 والسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

604
00:45:35,128 --> 00:45:39,613
The two key things in this letter is number one, that Heraclius is in Antioch.

605
00:45:41,074 --> 00:45:44,210
So he telling the Khalifah(خليفه) that Heracul(هراقل) is taking this so serious,

606
00:45:44,723 --> 00:45:52,180
he moved out of his capital, Constantinople, and he came to Antioch to be close to the field of operations.

607
00:45:52,370 --> 00:45:54,338
So the Romans are taking this very seriously.

608
00:45:54,772 --> 00:46:00,465
The second thing, is that he sent out to the people of his kingdom, calling them and he said:

609
00:46:00,490 --> 00:46:02,236
فجاعه على صعب والذلول

610
00:46:02,268 --> 00:46:06,813
Meaning they flooded from every direction, huge numbers started descending on us.

611
00:46:06,834 --> 00:46:08,657
So these are the two things in the letter.

612
00:46:09,767 --> 00:46:12,211
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he sent a letter back,

613
00:46:13,008 --> 00:46:15,629
he said: In the Name of Allah, the Compassionate, the Merciful.

614
00:46:16,149 --> 00:46:19,918
I received your letter about what Heraclius the king of the Romans has done.

615
00:46:20,813 --> 00:46:24,997
In regards to his establishing, setting base in Antioch,

616
00:46:25,251 --> 00:46:27,986
It is his defeat and your victory.

617
00:46:28,452 --> 00:46:34,328
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is a leader, who has confidence in the victory of Allah.

618
00:46:35,594 --> 00:46:39,875
And he wants to emanate that confidence

619
00:46:40,258 --> 00:46:47,304
he wants that confidence to get into the hearts of a Sahabah رضي الله عنهم who are leading these battles.

620
00:46:48,649 --> 00:46:52,622
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is in charge of a very, very difficult campaign.

621
00:46:53,100 --> 00:46:55,284
First of all, because it's not the only thing he's doing.

622
00:46:55,671 --> 00:46:59,683
He is running two separate campaigns, one against the Persian Empire in Iraq,

623
00:47:00,031 --> 00:47:02,652
and the second one against the Romans in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

624
00:47:03,067 --> 00:47:06,414
So he's having to deal with two different fronts in the same time.

625
00:47:06,629 --> 00:47:10,137
Number two, he's running very, very low in terms of resources.

626
00:47:10,278 --> 00:47:16,118
He doesn't have any more people(men), and in terms of the finances, the Treasury is bankrupt.

627
00:47:17,157 --> 00:47:19,782
So the situation is very difficult on Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

628
00:47:19,807 --> 00:47:25,116
And this is a situation where only a very, very strong hearted leader could deal with.

629
00:47:26,652 --> 00:47:29,254
First of all, this is a voluntary thing, he didn't have to send these armies.

630
00:47:30,363 --> 00:47:35,345
The Romans were not an eminent threat, on Madina, he could have waited,

631
00:47:35,803 --> 00:47:39,431
but Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه does not want a moment to pass

632
00:47:39,685 --> 00:47:42,255
without him spreading the message of Allah and we read

633
00:47:42,490 --> 00:47:45,103
his instructions to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) in our previous session.

634
00:47:45,482 --> 00:47:48,397
He is telling Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and look at what I have done

635
00:47:48,421 --> 00:47:50,709
the exact day the Messenger of Allah has passed away.

636
00:47:51,182 --> 00:47:57,729
Meaning don't let any catastrophe divert you from what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has appointed you to,

637
00:47:58,432 --> 00:48:02,687
even though the Messenger of Allah has died, and that's the greatest disaster to befall us.

638
00:48:03,163 --> 00:48:05,531
I would still working on the issue of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

639
00:48:05,883 --> 00:48:08,606
Three days later, I'm sending out the army of Osama(أسامة).

640
00:48:08,961 --> 00:48:15,220
So, he is telling Umar(عُمَر) don't let a moment pass you by without fulfilling your role in Da'wah(دعوة) and Jihad(جهاد).

641
00:48:16,532 --> 00:48:23,642
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه wants to give good hope and confidence

642
00:48:24,609 --> 00:48:27,796
to Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح) and the other Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

643
00:48:27,821 --> 00:48:31,797
So, he tells him: When you say that Heracul(هراقل) is an Antakiya(أنتاكية)

644
00:48:32,270 --> 00:48:37,223
that's good news for you that he is going to be defeated and you will be victorious.

645
00:48:37,517 --> 00:48:42,754
If he is taking it so seriously, that means that he's afraid and this is for our benefit.

646
00:48:42,965 --> 00:48:46,165
So that's not something to terrify me with.

647
00:48:46,371 --> 00:48:51,434
That's, in fact, good news, in my view, it also shows you the positiveness of the Sahabah(صحابه).

648
00:48:52,974 --> 00:48:56,341
Something that will be taken by others as an evil omen,

649
00:48:56,591 --> 00:49:00,612
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه sees it as Fa'al Al-Hasan(فعل الحسن), it's good news.

650
00:49:01,551 --> 00:49:05,604
And then, regarding what you mentioned about the Romans assembling for you,

651
00:49:05,629 --> 00:49:11,167
the people of their empire and massing for you, huge armies

652
00:49:11,913 --> 00:49:14,526
is something that we, and you already knew would happen.

653
00:49:15,288 --> 00:49:17,529
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is trying to tell him, what's the news in that?

654
00:49:18,054 --> 00:49:21,134
He didn't tell me anything new. We and you,

655
00:49:21,345 --> 00:49:23,868
قد كنَّا نحن أنتم تعلمون أنَّه حاصل

656
00:49:24,295 --> 00:49:27,871
We and you, already knew that this is expected and this would happen and then he said;

657
00:49:28,689 --> 00:49:33,317
A people would not give up their reign and leave their kingdom without the fight.

658
00:49:34,235 --> 00:49:37,626
Do you think that the Romans just walk out and give you Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)?

659
00:49:37,680 --> 00:49:40,985
What do you expect, they're gonna fight you with one or two soldiers.?

660
00:49:41,159 --> 00:49:43,534
It only makes sense that they will do this and even more.

661
00:49:43,987 --> 00:49:45,835
So he said: You're not telling me anything new.

662
00:49:47,916 --> 00:49:50,929
You should have already known better that they will do their best to fight you.

663
00:49:51,352 --> 00:49:53,642
Because people are not going to give up their reign

664
00:49:53,697 --> 00:49:57,802
and walk out of the kingdom without fighting, this is something expected

665
00:49:58,621 --> 00:50:02,719
and it's the price you have to pay for Jihad(جهاد) and Da'wah(دعوة) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عزوجل).

666
00:50:03,676 --> 00:50:10,683
And then he told him: And you know that attacking them are men, who love death,

667
00:50:11,101 --> 00:50:12,945
just as they love life,

668
00:50:13,507 --> 00:50:17,573
and they love Jihad(جهاد) more than they love virgin woman and wealth.

669
00:50:17,984 --> 00:50:20,925
One man of these is stronger than 1000 of the enemy.

670
00:50:21,266 --> 00:50:23,533
So face your enemy with your soldiers,

671
00:50:23,711 --> 00:50:28,004
and do not feel in need of Muslims who are not with you, because Allah is with you.

672
00:50:28,392 --> 00:50:30,576
He is telling him: Don't ask me for any reinforcements.

673
00:50:31,255 --> 00:50:35,452
Don't expect any Muslims, who are not with you to join you, because Allah is with you.

674
00:50:36,051 --> 00:50:38,558
Don't look forward for that to happen.

675
00:50:40,013 --> 00:50:43,001
So he's establishing the Aqeedah(عقيدة) in the hearts of Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة).

676
00:50:43,483 --> 00:50:46,051
That Allah is with you and you don't need anybody else.

677
00:50:47,021 --> 00:50:49,068
But then he turns around and he says;

678
00:50:49,450 --> 00:50:53,557
Nevertheless, I will still reinforce you until you're satisfied.

679
00:50:54,353 --> 00:50:57,614
Don't expect it. Don't look forward to it. Put your trust in Allah.

680
00:50:57,939 --> 00:51:00,868
Nevertheless, I'm going to send you a reinforcement until I make you happy.

681
00:51:02,907 --> 00:51:05,704
Obviously, when Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) reads such a letter to the Muslim soldiers,

682
00:51:05,728 --> 00:51:08,573
this is good news for them, this will uplift their spirits.

683
00:51:08,829 --> 00:51:12,285
Numbers, not a problem, one of us is equal 1000.

684
00:51:12,774 --> 00:51:14,247
Heracul(هراقل) in in Antakiya(أنتاكية),

685
00:51:14,732 --> 00:51:17,670
we should take that as good news that that's the end of his kingdom.

686
00:51:19,402 --> 00:51:25,672
It also shows you that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم did not expect people with especially the Romans,

687
00:51:26,212 --> 00:51:31,162
the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم knew that they're not just give up and hand over the land to you,

688
00:51:31,618 --> 00:51:34,574
without fighting and Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) in his advice he said;

689
00:51:34,599 --> 00:51:36,273
حدٌ حديد ورُكنٌ الشديد

690
00:51:37,074 --> 00:51:41,035
So they had a very practical view of life

691
00:51:41,222 --> 00:51:44,637
and how people are going to receive the Da'wah(دعوة) of Islam.

692
00:51:45,490 --> 00:51:49,698
Now, the four armies are in dilemma, the numbers are huge,

693
00:51:49,912 --> 00:51:53,035
and even though Al-Khalifah(خليفه) is giving them this boost,

694
00:51:53,483 --> 00:51:59,330
and he sent a letter to Yazeed(يزيد) for example, we just briefly go through the letter that he sent to your Yazeed(يزيد).

695
00:51:59,743 --> 00:52:05,148
 He said: Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله)  Allah! has given us victory in the time of Rasool Ullah

696
00:52:05,434 --> 00:52:07,878
 through putting fear in the hearts of the enemy,

697
00:52:08,067 --> 00:52:12,879
and He assisted us with angels and the One, Who assists us with angels

698
00:52:12,904 --> 00:52:18,395
and assisted us with putting fear in the hearts of the enemy is our Lord today.

699
00:52:19,340 --> 00:52:20,621
And we're fighting for the same purpose.

700
00:52:20,685 --> 00:52:26,526
Allah, Who assisted us yesterday is our Lord today and He will assist us today and tomorrow.

701
00:52:27,015 --> 00:52:29,566
He's telling Yazeed(يزيد) about things that Yazeed(يزيد) did not witness.

702
00:52:30,156 --> 00:52:36,428
Yazeed(يزيد) was a late Muslim. He did not attend Badr(بدر) on the side of the Muslims.

703
00:52:36,939 --> 00:52:39,868
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was telling him, in those days we didn't have numbers

704
00:52:41,127 --> 00:52:42,965
but Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has still given us victory.

705
00:52:43,324 --> 00:52:45,852
So don't worry about the numbers that you're mentioning to me.

706
00:52:46,762 --> 00:52:49,473
And then he said: And the ones, who bear witness that Allah is One

707
00:52:49,746 --> 00:52:53,611
are not like the ones, who associate other gods with Allah.

708
00:52:54,178 --> 00:52:57,882
And then he said that a small group can gain victory over a large group,

709
00:52:58,209 --> 00:53:01,548
if they have Taqwa(تقوى) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, and then he also told him in the end,

710
00:53:01,581 --> 00:53:04,036
and I will assist you with some reinforcements,

711
00:53:04,345 --> 00:53:06,791
and then he responded to the letter of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

712
00:53:07,242 --> 00:53:11,610
He said: You telling me that the Romans have gathered to you and assembled large armies,

713
00:53:11,914 --> 00:53:16,696
but Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has never given us victory, during the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ through numbers.

714
00:53:17,722 --> 00:53:21,034
We used to fight with Rasool Allah ﷺ and we only had two horses

715
00:53:21,588 --> 00:53:24,408
and we used to take turns on riding our camels.

716
00:53:25,198 --> 00:53:27,210
In the battle of Uhud(أحَد), we only had one horse.

717
00:53:27,531 --> 00:53:31,935
Rasool Allah ﷺ would ride it and then he would give it to some of us.

718
00:53:32,633 --> 00:53:39,112
And then he told Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) that you and your army should stay away from sins.

719
00:53:40,509 --> 00:53:42,523
So these were the Naseeha(نَصيحة) of Al-Khalifah(خليفه).

720
00:53:42,584 --> 00:53:45,061
Now, what's the plan?

721
00:53:45,260 --> 00:53:48,433
What was the plan of Al-Khalifah(خليفه), how to deal with this situation?

722
00:53:48,724 --> 00:53:49,918
Things are now different.

723
00:53:50,096 --> 00:53:53,842
The armies are faced with a huge opponent.

724
00:53:54,917 --> 00:54:03,220
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) even though he told his commanders in the field to seek no assistance from anyone but Allah

725
00:54:03,260 --> 00:54:04,807
 and don't expect reinforcements.

726
00:54:05,399 --> 00:54:09,261
He feels that there is still a need to reinforce these armies.

727
00:54:09,723 --> 00:54:15,555
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) realizes that, but he has no other soldiers.

728
00:54:16,073 --> 00:54:20,635
He has squeezed Yemen and brought out the tribes of Himyar(حمير)

729
00:54:20,745 --> 00:54:23,886
 and Kinda(كندة) and Hazara Moat(حضرالموت) and they're all set out.

730
00:54:25,340 --> 00:54:26,909
Where else can he get soldiers from?

731
00:54:28,123 --> 00:54:33,685
The only thing he could come up with, is to ask Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

732
00:54:34,357 --> 00:54:40,071
to split up the arm in Iraq and set out to reinforce the Muslims in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

733
00:54:40,156 --> 00:54:41,634
That's the only thing he could do.

734
00:54:42,785 --> 00:54:44,626
That's the only resource, he has left.

735
00:54:45,387 --> 00:54:50,820
Obviously, by doing that he would weaken the Muslims in Iraq,

736
00:54:51,051 --> 00:54:53,271
because he will only leave behind half of the forces.

737
00:54:53,606 --> 00:54:57,161
But he felt that that's a temporary sacrifice that he could afford.

738
00:54:57,228 --> 00:55:02,259
And he wanted the this army to go to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) finish off the job in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)

739
00:55:02,284 --> 00:55:05,250
and to immediately return to Iraq, where they belong.

740
00:55:05,837 --> 00:55:10,441
And we talked about this splitting of the army in the last session

741
00:55:10,466 --> 00:55:12,922
between Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and Al-Muthanna Bin Harissa(ألمثنى بن حارثه)

742
00:55:13,387 --> 00:55:18,068
but we didn't talk about how Khalid(خالد) got from Iraq to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

743
00:55:18,417 --> 00:55:23,105
Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه received this letter from the Khalifah(خليفه)

744
00:55:23,329 --> 00:55:27,709
telling him, immediately to go and rescue the Muslims of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)

745
00:55:28,514 --> 00:55:30,717
and that was after the Hajj(حَجْ) of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

746
00:55:30,738 --> 00:55:34,125
in which Al-Khalifah(خليفه) reprimanded Khalid(خالد) for it, and told him never do that again.

747
00:55:34,290 --> 00:55:38,790
And then he told him because no one will relieve the distress of the Muslims like you

748
00:55:39,383 --> 00:55:42,198
and no one will crack the enemy and break them like you.

749
00:55:42,762 --> 00:55:44,221
So don't do something like that again.

750
00:55:45,492 --> 00:55:49,847
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) receives this letter and he feels the urgency of the situation.

751
00:55:49,868 --> 00:55:51,851
He must get to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) immediately,

752
00:55:52,252 --> 00:55:58,110
because these four Roman armies are descending on the Muslims as fast as they can.

753
00:55:58,479 --> 00:56:02,239
And if he doesn't make it in time, it will be too late. But the problem is

754
00:56:02,375 --> 00:56:08,915
all of the routes that connect Al-Iraq(ألعراق) to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) are lined up by Roman Garrisons.

755
00:56:09,430 --> 00:56:15,580
So if he is going to take those traditional routes, he must fight with these Garrison's

756
00:56:15,724 --> 00:56:21,588
and that will hold him back and delay his assistance to the Muslims in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

757
00:56:22,513 --> 00:56:25,694
And he needs to get there immediately. So he gathered all of his guides,

758
00:56:25,970 --> 00:56:31,123
the guides in the desert because Yani(يعني) the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم don’t know this territory,

759
00:56:31,147 --> 00:56:34,949
so they have guides, local people, he gathered them all he told them,

760
00:56:35,260 --> 00:56:39,259
This is what I need to do! I need to go behind all of the Roman lines.

761
00:56:40,150 --> 00:56:43,591
And I need to dig deep into Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) without meeting any resistance.

762
00:56:44,119 --> 00:56:45,595
They told him: There's no way to do that.

763
00:56:46,103 --> 00:56:47,794
These are the traditional routes.

764
00:56:48,754 --> 00:56:52,150
This is all what we can offer you, he said: You have to do me something!

765
00:56:52,603 --> 00:56:53,730
Find me another way.

766
00:56:53,879 --> 00:56:55,270
They said: There isn't another way

767
00:56:56,233 --> 00:56:59,045
because the only other way which is crossing the desert

768
00:56:59,536 --> 00:57:04,147
is a path that was never ever crossed before by an army

769
00:57:04,451 --> 00:57:09,718
and it's a path that even if a lone traveler takes, he still fears on his life.

770
00:57:10,667 --> 00:57:12,905
You know sometimes a lone traveler can make it

771
00:57:12,984 --> 00:57:17,327
but it's only the best of them and it's very risky

772
00:57:17,474 --> 00:57:22,964
but for entire army loaded with weapons and equipment

773
00:57:23,334 --> 00:57:26,301
it's an impossible feat and nobody has ever done it before.

774
00:57:26,428 --> 00:57:28,821
The Romans have been here for centuries and they never did it.

775
00:57:28,880 --> 00:57:32,548
The Persians have been in this land for some time they never did it, nobody did it before.

776
00:57:32,896 --> 00:57:38,448
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: That's the only way tell me how to do it.?

777
00:57:39,253 --> 00:57:42,766
None of the guides was willing to bear that responsibility.

778
00:57:42,791 --> 00:57:46,055
They said: It will be a disaster for the Muslims, Mahlakah(محلكة).

779
00:57:46,617 --> 00:57:51,833
The Muslims will perish, except for one of the guides, Rafiya Bin Umair(رافع بن عمير).

780
00:57:52,103 --> 00:57:54,165
He said: I could help you with that.

781
00:57:54,782 --> 00:57:57,771
Now the Muslims were discussing this with Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد),

782
00:57:58,947 --> 00:58:03,838
it is a major feat it couldn't be a disaster on the entire army.

783
00:58:04,993 --> 00:58:07,442
Half of the forces in Iraq could perish in the desert.

784
00:58:07,813 --> 00:58:10,867
The guides have given Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) their opinion.

785
00:58:11,234 --> 00:58:13,074
They told him: You can't do it.

786
00:58:13,249 --> 00:58:15,471
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) responded by saying;

787
00:58:15,724 --> 00:58:22,731
ان المسلم ينبغي اَلَا يكترس بشيء يقى فيه مع ماعونت الله له

788
00:58:23,200 --> 00:58:28,019
He said: The Muslim should not care about anything, he does.

789
00:58:28,531 --> 00:58:31,733
If he has the assistance of Allah on his side.

790
00:58:32,820 --> 00:58:35,201
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was willing to take the risk.

791
00:58:35,447 --> 00:58:40,827
 He was audacious and such an enterprising person, he was willing to take this risk

792
00:58:40,867 --> 00:58:49,894
 and is telling the guides and the army that we should not bother, we should not care at all about anything,

793
00:58:50,221 --> 00:58:52,050
if Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is with us.

794
00:58:52,645 --> 00:58:55,161
Tell me what we could do, and we'll do it.

795
00:58:55,840 --> 00:59:00,929
Rafiya Bin Umair(رافع بن عمير) stands up and said: O Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد),

796
00:59:01,311 --> 00:59:04,768
if you insist on us doing that, this is what we have to do.

797
00:59:04,792 --> 00:59:09,878
I want you to give me the strongest 20 camels that you have in the army.

798
00:59:10,566 --> 00:59:13,667
So he handed them over, he deprived them from water

799
00:59:14,128 --> 00:59:17,054
and then when they were very thirsty, he gave them a lot of water to drink.

800
00:59:17,503 --> 00:59:24,337
And then he cut off their lips, mask the mouth and also prevented them from urinating

801
00:59:24,745 --> 00:59:29,257
and he made sure that every soldier in the Army has transportation,

802
00:59:29,582 --> 00:59:34,963
and he told them to load up five days worth of water Bismillah( بسم الله) let's start.

803
00:59:36,050 --> 00:59:39,971
And they started from Qaraqir(قراقر) and their destination was Suwaa(سوَّى).

804
00:59:40,451 --> 00:59:46,123
Five days travel without any source of water and without any settlements along the way.

805
00:59:46,693 --> 00:59:50,411
It is a very rough terrain, desert no one lives there

806
00:59:50,563 --> 00:59:54,582
five days you're not gonna see anyone if you make it, from Qaraqir(قراقر) to Suwaa(سوَّى).

807
00:59:54,782 --> 00:59:58,119
Then after that there are settlements that you could survive on.

808
00:59:58,437 --> 01:00:01,587
But you have to make this segment which is five days long,

809
01:00:01,888 --> 01:00:03,563
without any supplements whatsoever.

810
01:00:04,708 --> 01:00:06,931
They started the journey Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

811
01:00:07,114 --> 01:00:09,964
planned it in a way that they would travel double the distance

812
01:00:10,504 --> 01:00:12,875
by traveling at night and traveling in the morning.

813
01:00:13,232 --> 01:00:14,518
 You have to put more effort in it.

814
01:00:14,785 --> 01:00:17,777
And they went through this rough terrain this desert,

815
01:00:18,121 --> 01:00:21,486
under the guidance of Rafiya Bin Umair(رافع بن عمير).

816
01:00:21,756 --> 01:00:27,779
After five days, they ran out of their water those 20 camels that were packed with water,

817
01:00:28,318 --> 01:00:33,092
they would slaughter them and empty the stomach contents and give it to the horses,

818
01:00:33,117 --> 01:00:37,892
so the horses would drink from what's in the inside of the camels

819
01:00:38,239 --> 01:00:40,993
and then the soldiers would drink from their supplies of water.

820
01:00:41,716 --> 01:00:46,446
After five days Rafiya(رافع) has told them, you will find sources of water there will be some water.

821
01:00:47,481 --> 01:00:53,907
But he couldn't see it, because he got this disease in his eyes, which temporarily blinded him.

822
01:00:54,586 --> 01:00:57,927
So now, five days are over, we don't have any water left.

823
01:00:57,992 --> 01:00:59,516
Tell us where the water is.

824
01:01:00,009 --> 01:01:01,253
The guide cannot see.

825
01:01:02,213 --> 01:01:04,419
They tell him: Come on, you have to do something for us.

826
01:01:04,983 --> 01:01:08,403
He said: Alright, look for this particular tree.

827
01:01:09,372 --> 01:01:11,261
And he told them that particular species.

828
01:01:11,560 --> 01:01:14,675
They went looking for it they couldn't find it. He said: Look for it.

829
01:01:15,251 --> 01:01:19,838
Again, they went to look but then they found it but the tree was already chopped.

830
01:01:20,024 --> 01:01:21,387
So they found the trunk of it.

831
01:01:21,641 --> 01:01:24,054
He said: Dig next to the tree.

832
01:01:24,284 --> 01:01:30,343
And when they were digging, they came to some spring of water.

833
01:01:30,979 --> 01:01:37,376
He told them: I've never been here except once and that was with my father 30 years ago.

834
01:01:38,966 --> 01:01:41,915
So he remembered the tree and remembered that there was water there

835
01:01:41,966 --> 01:01:45,359
but he has never been there for over 30 years and he said:

836
01:01:45,384 --> 01:01:48,896
He refreshed in his mind remembered where the water would be

837
01:01:49,211 --> 01:01:51,595
even though he was temporarily blind,

838
01:01:51,620 --> 01:01:53,822
that it could have been because of the Sun in the desert sometimes

839
01:01:54,150 --> 01:01:57,184
it cause you to lose your sight because of the reflection of light

840
01:01:57,209 --> 01:01:59,207
on the sand if it's bright in color.

841
01:01:59,723 --> 01:02:04,712
So they reached and there was a some poetry made about that,

842
01:02:05,095 --> 01:02:07,850
لِلَّهِ دَرُّ رافِعٍ أَنّى اِهتَدى

843
01:02:08,159 --> 01:02:10,251
 فَوَّزَ مِن قَراقِرٍ إِلى سُوى

844
01:02:10,518 --> 01:02:12,754
خِمْسًا إِذَا سَارَ بِهِ الْجِبْسُ بَكَى

845
01:02:12,979 --> 01:02:15,420
ما سَارها من قبله إنسٌ يُرى

846
01:02:16,233 --> 01:02:19,460
May Allah reward Rafiya(رافع), How was he guided

847
01:02:20,022 --> 01:02:23,331
to travel from Qaraqir(قراقر) all the way to Suwaa(سوى),

848
01:02:23,694 --> 01:02:27,337
five days if any army marches through it, it would cry.

849
01:02:27,647 --> 01:02:29,797
No one ever marched there before you.

850
01:02:29,993 --> 01:02:34,458
So this was the first time ever this happened.

851
01:02:34,901 --> 01:02:39,459
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) is now in the depth of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

852
01:02:39,988 --> 01:02:42,809
It was a surprise for the Romans.

853
01:02:43,090 --> 01:02:45,235
How could he make it with such speed?

854
01:02:45,371 --> 01:02:50,360
How could he make it unnoticed what happened to all of our Garrison's on the way

855
01:02:50,928 --> 01:02:52,724
the Romans have been there for centuries.

856
01:02:52,749 --> 01:02:55,763
They know what the traditional routes are, they are all protected.

857
01:02:56,162 --> 01:03:00,142
And now suddenly they find Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) with his army in their midst,

858
01:03:00,446 --> 01:03:04,030
and they already have heard about the reputation of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

859
01:03:04,225 --> 01:03:05,541
So for them, this was a miracle.

860
01:03:06,156 --> 01:03:09,143
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) whom they've been hearing about all of these stories

861
01:03:09,468 --> 01:03:11,412
and now their stories were confirmed.

862
01:03:11,601 --> 01:03:15,468
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) landed out of nowhere in the middle of our land,

863
01:03:15,762 --> 01:03:18,040
with such speed and unnoticed.

864
01:03:18,207 --> 01:03:20,691
And that struck fear in their hearts.

865
01:03:21,152 --> 01:03:22,646
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) gets into Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)

866
01:03:22,865 --> 01:03:25,400
and he is now ready to reinforce the Muslims.

867
01:03:26,092 --> 01:03:32,648
The plan was, we should not fight them separately, four armies are easier to take on than one.

868
01:03:33,124 --> 01:03:35,684
So he told the Muslim armies to join together.

869
01:03:36,001 --> 01:03:39,707
He said: When your numbers are small don't fight the enemy separately.

870
01:03:39,906 --> 01:03:41,326
Bring your numbers together.

871
01:03:42,543 --> 01:03:48,211
So the three armies were told to withdraw from all of the territory that they occupied.

872
01:03:48,552 --> 01:03:52,587
Leave Damascus! Leave Hims(حمص)! Just come back all the way to Yarmook(يرموك),

873
01:03:53,130 --> 01:03:54,466
which is in present day Jordan.

874
01:03:54,713 --> 01:03:58,782
So that will be the battlefield where they would meet the army of the Romans.

875
01:03:59,134 --> 01:04:03,598
Three armies succeeded in withdrawing the army Yazeed(يزيد), the army of Sharhabil(شرحبيل)

876
01:04:04,000 --> 01:04:06,082
and the army of Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة).

877
01:04:06,316 --> 01:04:10,738
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) got bogged down in Falastine(فلسطين)

878
01:04:11,355 --> 01:04:14,867
because the distance between him and the Roman army was so short,

879
01:04:15,246 --> 01:04:19,067
he cannot turn away his back without being hit from the rear.

880
01:04:19,665 --> 01:04:22,049
So he had to maneuver slowly and slowly.

881
01:04:22,610 --> 01:04:24,700
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) had two choices,

882
01:04:25,590 --> 01:04:29,790
either to tell Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) to withdraw and suffer the consequences

883
01:04:30,145 --> 01:04:34,128
or he goes in and joins hands with Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص)

884
01:04:34,475 --> 01:04:39,830
and they give the Roman army a shot, which was 90,000 Strong.

885
01:04:40,217 --> 01:04:43,964
Khalid(خالد) went with the latter, so he rushed into Falastine(فلسطين)

886
01:04:44,402 --> 01:04:49,807
joined hands with Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and they fought the battle of Ajnadeen(أجنادين),

887
01:04:50,003 --> 01:04:55,535
which was a great victory for the Muslims and a disaster to the Romans.

888
01:04:55,883 --> 01:05:00,521
The news reached to Heracles, he said: This is the beginning of our defeat.

889
01:05:01,131 --> 01:05:04,660
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and Amr(عمر) they withdrew to Al-Yarmook(أليرموك).

890
01:05:04,988 --> 01:05:08,016
Now Heracul(هراقل) is already sensing the danger.

891
01:05:08,506 --> 01:05:14,326
And he knows that his soldiers are gonna have a hard time standing up against the Muslims.

892
01:05:14,630 --> 01:05:17,488
So what he told his generals he said;

893
01:05:17,860 --> 01:05:24,351
Choose a battleground that is very wide from the front, but is very narrow from the back

894
01:05:24,805 --> 01:05:28,959
in order to refuse our soldiers the option of retreating.

895
01:05:30,678 --> 01:05:33,939
He saw that this is the only way to deal with these Muslims.

896
01:05:34,428 --> 01:05:36,134
Our soldiers cannot stand in front of them.

897
01:05:36,575 --> 01:05:40,127
So they chose Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), they chose a position of Yarmook(يرموك)

898
01:05:40,317 --> 01:05:43,826
in front of them was an open plan and behind them was a cliff.

899
01:05:45,677 --> 01:05:48,804
So obviously, you can't run away, a cliff is behind you.

900
01:05:50,376 --> 01:05:52,298
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) as soon as he saw that, he said;

901
01:05:52,323 --> 01:05:57,442
أبشرو قد جَآء نصر فولله قلَّى ما يعتي محصورٌ بخير

902
01:05:58,064 --> 01:05:59,000
He said; Rejoice.

903
01:05:59,040 --> 01:06:01,913
Look at the positiveness of the Sahabah(صحابه) they would make a good news out of anything.

904
01:06:02,357 --> 01:06:05,186
 Rejoice! Victory is on its way

905
01:06:05,535 --> 01:06:11,028
because they have cornered themselves and rarely does a cornered man ever survive.

906
01:06:11,538 --> 01:06:14,996
You've cornered yourself, you chose to put yourself in that position.

907
01:06:15,233 --> 01:06:18,411
Rarely has anybody who has done that come out with any good.

908
01:06:18,853 --> 01:06:25,579
The enemy was 250,000, While the Muslims when they joined together were 40,000

909
01:06:27,044 --> 01:06:30,144
and that is a Battle of Al-Yarmook(أليرموك)

910
01:06:30,168 --> 01:06:33,246
which we will talk about in sha Allah Ta'ala(إنشاء الله تعالى) Monday.

911
01:06:34,716 --> 01:06:37,980
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

